 If `Map.groupBy` is unavailable for being too new, the alternative is to use `Array#reduce` to acbieve the same result and group the results into a map

```
$(":input", el).serializeArray()
 .reduce(
 (map, data) => {
 //create initial group if not there
 if (!map.has(data.name))
 map.set(data.name, []);

 // add to the existing group
 const currentGroup = map.get(data.name);
 currentGroup.push(data);
 return map;
 },
 new Map()
)

```

 And if `Iterator#map` is unavailable, then a suitable alternative to `iterator.map(mappingFunction)` is `Array.from(iterator, mappingFunction)`. See also Using map() on an iterator and in particular using a generator function (and here ) which more closely matches `Iterator#map` since it is lazily evaluated.

