 Edit

 String enums look different than regular ones, for example:

```
enum MyEnum {
 A = "a",
 B = "b",
 C = "c"
}

```

 Compiles into:

```
var MyEnum;
(function (MyEnum) {
 MyEnum["A"] = "a";
 MyEnum["B"] = "b";
 MyEnum["C"] = "c";
})(MyEnum || (MyEnum = {}));

