solution:
`baseUrl` will no longer be supported in Typescript 7.0 as explained in this related GitHub post by Daniel Rosenwasser.

 To fix the error, explicitly include the full path in your `paths` mappings. As an example, instead of

```
// old file with baseUrl
{
 "compilerOptions": {
 "baseUrl": "./src",
 "paths": {
 "@app/*": ["app/*"],
 "@lib/*": ["lib/*"]
 }
 }
}

```

 remove `baseUrl`, and the paths should become:

```
"paths": {
 // add ./src from baseUrl
 "@app/*": ["./src/app/*"],
 "@lib/*": ["./src/lib/*"]
}

```

